    "description": "For a monotone directed family of subsets/subrings and an arbitrary index type kappa, conjecture that the kappa-power functor commutes with the directed union (colimit) if and only if every kappa-indexed family of germs has finite essential support relative to the system, i.e. kappa is finite or the coordinates are constrained to a finitely-supported subspace, with no intermediate regime. The mechanism is that directedness absorbs any finite set of stages into a single one but is powerless against an infinite one, so the obstruction is concentrated entirely in the cardinality of the active index set. Approach: prove both implications, using a finite-upper-bound argument for the sufficiency direction and an unboundedness witness (analogous to the identity sequence on the standard exhaustion) for the necessity direction.",
